  "gradeRuleDescribe": {
    "yms_year": 114.0,
    "yms_smester": 1.0,
    "cls_id": "CB06310",
    "sub_id": "26210",
    "scr_dup": "001",
    "tpa_score_new": "<div>Attendance and Participation 30% Homework 35% Term Paper Presentation 35% 針對網路修課同學 每週作業 65% 期末報告 35%</div>\n",
    "tpa_score_new_en": " ",
    "course_pol": "期中考、期末考與小考若當日若無法參加考試，務必於考試前事先告知(因學校請假系統無法得知同學申請時間，請各位主動善加利用ilearn2.0訊息功能、mail等) 。\n若有事先告知者，才可以請老師與助教聯繫與安排補考時間，補考時間必須安排在三日內完成(補考成績將打8折)。\n若無收到老師與實習助教聯繫，請與我們再次確認請假問題。\n其他規定將依照實際上課情況調整，請同學們務必專心上課喔!!!",
    "course_pol_en": "If you are unable to attend the midterm exam, final exam, or quiz on the day, you must inform us in advance before the exam (because the school leave system cannot know the time of student application, please take the initiative to make full use of the ilearn2.0 messaging function, email, etc.).\nOnly if you are notified in advance, you can ask the teacher to contact the teaching assistant to arrange the make-up test time. The make-up test time must be arranged within three days (the make-up test results will be discounted by 20%).\nIf you do not receive any contact from the teacher or the internship teaching assistant, please confirm with us about your leave request.\nOther regulations will be adjusted according to the actual class situation. Please be sure to concentrate on class!!!",
    "course_rem": null,
    "course_rem_en": null,
    "ais_meno": "<div>在作業與課程討論中，我強烈鼓勵同學們合作完成作業與課程討論的學習任務。然而，請注意，當我們撰寫作業與課程討論時，我們必須嚴格遵守有關確認語詞和想法來源的標準規則。如果我們使用其他作者或網路文章的用語或想法，必須清楚標示這些用語或想法的來源，並在作業與課程討論中提供這些素材的出處。這包括作者的姓名以及在句子末尾包含使用原材料的頁碼。如果我們抄襲或以任何方式隱藏我們作品的來源，我們的作業將被視為零分。</div>\n",
    "ais_meno_en": "<div>In assignments and course discussions, I strongly encourage students to cooperate in completing the learning tasks of assignments and course discussions. However, please note that when we write assignments and course discussions, we must strictly adhere to standard rules about identifying the sources of words and ideas. If we use words or ideas from other authors or online articles, we must clearly identify the source of these words or ideas and provide the source of the material in assignments and course discussions. This includes the author&#39;s name and, at the end of the sentence, the page number where the source material was used. If we plagiarize or hide the origin of our work in any way, our assignment will be considered a zero.</div>\n",
    "ilearn_mk": null
  },
